title: Finance & Commerce
subtitle: Trade policy, the guilds, the Banking Clan and the treasury.
is-card: true
tags: senate_affairs
card-image: img/card_credits.svg
view-if: finance_timer <= 0 and chair_finance = "rc" and cardok_finance
on-arrival: turn_actions += 1; finance_timer = 3; last_card_timer = "finance"
new-page: true

= Finance & Commerce Committee

The Caucus chairs the Finance & Commerce Committee. The Republic treasury stands at [+ treasury +].

- @regulate: Regulate the trade guilds.
- @breakup: Break up the Trade Federation.
- @audit: Audit the InterGalactic Banking Clan.
- @independent: Guarantee the Banking Clan's independence from the Chancellery.
- @books: Balance the Republic's books.
- @easy_discard

@regulate
view-if: corruption > 25 and guild_relation > 5
subtitle: Less corruption; the guilds retaliate.
on-arrival: guild_relation -= 8; corruption -= 1.5; guild_embargo += 1; corporate_sep += 2; rim_hardship -= 1

New disclosure rules for guild lobbying pass in committee. The guilds call it persecution.

@breakup
view-if: not tf_broken_up and (gunray_convicted or evidence >= 4 or naboo_free)
subtitle: −2 political capital. A historic blow to the guilds, and a provocation to the corporate worlds.
choose-if: capital >= 2 and rc_in_govt
unavailable-subtitle: Needs 2 political capital and a seat in government.
on-arrival: {!
Q.capital -= 2;
var st = SW.stance(Q, {mod: 0.55, guild: 0, rim: 0.85, sec: 0.45, ind: 0.55, pal: 0.35, cis: 0}, true);
Q.tfb_vote = SW.vote(Q, st, 1, 'regulate');
Q.vote_html = SW.voteBanner('Trade Federation Dissolution Act', Q.tfb_vote);
if (Q.tfb_vote >= 50) { Q.tf_broken_up = 1; Q.corporate_guild -= 12; Q.guild_embargo += 3; Q.corporate_sep += 6; Q.corruption -= 3; Q.rim_relation += 6; this.achieve('trust_buster'); }
else { Q.guild_relation -= 6; }
!}

[+ vote_html +]

[? if tf_broken_up : The Trade Federation is to be broken into a dozen competing shipping concerns. The Neimoidians are apoplectic. The corporate worlds are frightened, and frightened worlds listen to separatists. ?][? if not tf_broken_up : The guilds' friends close ranks. The bill dies on the floor. ?]

@audit
view-if: not banking_audit
subtitle: A chance to find where the Republic's dark money flows.
on-arrival: banking_audit = 1; evidence += 0.8; guild_relation -= 4; banking_reformed += 0.5

The audit of the Banking Clan's Coruscant branch turns up loans to the Trade Federation guaranteed by Damask Holdings. Its founder, a Muun named Hego Damask, died in 32 BBY. His holding company kept spending money for years afterwards.

@independent
view-if: not banking_independent and date >= 120
subtitle: Blocks the Chancellery from seizing control of the banks in wartime.
choose-if: capital >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough political capital.
on-arrival: {!
Q.capital -= 1;
var st = SW.stance(Q, {mod: 0.6, guild: 0.75, rim: 0.5, sec: 0.35, ind: 0.55, pal: 0.15, cis: 0.6}, true);
Q.bi_vote = SW.vote(Q, st, 1, 'oversight');
Q.vote_html = SW.voteBanner('Banking Independence Act', Q.bi_vote);
if (Q.bi_vote >= 50) { Q.banking_independent = 1; Q.guild_relation += 4; }
!}

[+ vote_html +]

[? if banking_independent : The Banking Clan's charter now forbids any transfer of control to the executive. Nobody in [+ pal_office +] admits to ever wanting any such thing. ?][? if not banking_independent and not rc_chancellor : The bill fails. The Chancellor's allies say it "ties the Republic's hands in wartime". ?][? if not banking_independent and rc_chancellor : The bill fails. The guilds and the Security Bloc say it "ties the Republic's hands in wartime". ?]

@books
view-if: treasury < 6
subtitle: +2 treasury; the Rim feels the cuts.
on-arrival: treasury += 2; rim_hardship += 1.5; mod_relation += 2; rimward_dissent += 3

Spending is trimmed across the board. The Rim, as always, feels it first.
